    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Description:</b> </p>

<p>ODGB CP uses the boiler code provided by Pegasus, which uses Dropwizard internally. Dropwizards has two connectors - applicationConnectors and adminConnectors. Application requests are handled by applicationConnectors. Admin requests are handled by adminConnectors. Dropwizard separates connectors in config.yml. It uses the application for public access and the admin for internal (localhost-only) access. APIs defined using Application connectors have a filter called SPLAT mTLS filter that ensures the call is coming from SPLAT. If the user makes the call, then the user is authenticated with SPLAT, and SPLAT authenticates with the service. In case of admin-related tasks or APIs, the authentication to the admin interface is using TCP-based (port-based), which is weak.</p>

<p><b>Reasoning:</b></p>

<p>The implementation of the admin interface using TCP-based authentication is typically considered weak, as access control relies entirely on access to the port. Every process on the machine that has access to the port will be able to call the Admin API. This makes it hard to implement granular access control. An SSRF vulnerability could allow access to the privileged admin port from localhost, bypassing any network firewall or external restrictions and enabling the attacker to execute internal-only endpoints via the service. A misconfigured local app or service could access those ports and perform malicious actions. A Malicious operator with limited shell access might be able to connect to the API, violating the principle of least privilege. </p>

<p><b>Impact:</b></p>

<p>Unauthorized access can lead to the leakage of sensitive data, data manipulation, and service disruptions.</p>

<p><b>Note:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>This issue occurs on all OCI services that use the code provided by Pegasus - Dropwizard.</li>
	<li>Severity depends on the admin tasks provided by each service.</li>
	<li>New services use Micronaut, which is an in-house application developed by OCI that replaces Dropwizard. Not sure if the issue exists on Micronaut.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Mitigation:</b></p>

<p>Use project Forge to perform admin tasks</p>

<p><b>Instructions for Service Team:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Security Risk is marked by labels that <b>only SecArch should modify</b> - secarch-risk-level.</li>
	<li>This Security Risk finding will also appear in Security Central aligned with your supplied Phonebook entry.</li>
	<li>Prioritize remediation of this Security Risk in your SDLC in accordance with the <a href="https://confluence.oci.oraclecorp.com/x/2jBLAg" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">OCI SLA for Vulnerability Mitigations</a></li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
